cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. The paper that describes
  it is in preparation; this file will name it once it is public.
type: software
title: "bitdp: bit-parallel kernels for weighted linear-gap alignment, derived at compile time"
abstract: >-
  A Zig library that derives bit-parallel alignment kernels at compile time
  from a linear-gap scoring scheme, with the tests, benchmark harness and
  session logs behind the paper's numbers.
authors:
  - family-names: Tack
    given-names: James
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-5366-3544"
repository-code: "https://github.com/endlessconflict/bitdp"
url: "https://github.com/endlessconflict/bitdp"
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0-paper
keywords:
  - sequence alignment
  - bit-parallel dynamic programming
  - edit distance
  - SIMD
  - compile-time code generation
  - Zig
